{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6fb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a078f2-d5f9-7612-b470-6ad9a3cae55b"},"sequence":472,"recorded_at":1780531400000939,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"ba0fc865-f921-4c71-91f7-cd27de007268","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"ba0fc865-f921-4c71-91f7-cd27de007268","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"ba0fc865-f921-4c71-91f7-cd27de007268"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"25849b73-a4a7-42bf-a798-aab7d6dc33f8"},"task_id":"25849b73-a4a7-42bf-a798-aab7d6dc33f8","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"25849b73-a4a7-42bf-a798-aab7d6dc33f8","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-19-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cat \\\"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/TASK-260906-vmzk0y/rework-round3.md\\\" 2>/dev/null | head -n 60; echo ===DIRECTIVES===; task-board spawn directives \\\"$TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID\\\" 2>&1 | head -c 2000\",\n  \"description\": \"Read round-3 brief and directives\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"Rework round 3 of TASK-260906-vmzk0y. Worktree `.temp/STORY-260905-3t31e9/worktree`.\\nCHANGES REQUESTED — one blocking, and it was introduced **by** the round-2 fix.\\n\\nRound 2 closed all five findings and the reviewer re-verified every one\\nindependently rather than accepting the outcome: F1 and F2 refuse before\\naccumulating, driven through `ParseProviderDescriptor`, `New` and\\n`CheckVersionTuple`; F4 fails closed for a registered-but-unlifted code with\\nboth sub-arms pinned by different tests; F5's census scans every package file,\\nconst and var, grouped and typed, with all four plants confirmed by neutering\\nproduction behaviour; F3's rewritten bound reproduces in every sub-claim.\\nReviewer battery 23 applied / 23 killed, 0 survivors. Do not re-litigate any of\\nit.\\n\\n## G1 (blocking) — the saturation fix moved a refusal between classes\\n\\n`provhost/protocol.go:380`. The F2 fix saturates with an **early return**, which\\nexits `parseMajor` before the minor/patch validation at :386-395. So a version\\nwhose first component overflows is reported as a recognized major regardless of\\nwhat follows the dot:\\n\\n| Input | Classified as | Exit |\\n| --- | --- | ---: |\\n| `99999999999999999999.abc.def` | `incompatible_protocol` | 6 |\\n| `99999999999999999999.0.x` | `incompatible_protocol` | 6 |\\n| `18446744073709551618..0` | `incompatible_protocol` | 6 |\\n| `2.abc.def` | `provider_protocol_error` | **13** |\\n\\nTwo shipped doc comments say this must not happen — :359-360 (*anything else is\\nnot a recognizable major, so the frame is unusable rather than a mismatch*) and\\n:403-404 (*every other unusable frame yields provider_protocol_error*). The new\\nparagraph justifies the change with a narrower class than it enforces: it speaks\\nof an all-numeric giant, and these are not all-numeric.\\n\\n`foreignMajor` arms on the same predicate and skips the entire v2\\nmember-vocabulary check, so a bare frame carrying only `protocol` and\\n`protocol_version` refuses as `incompatible_protocol` for the malformed giant\\nbut as *missing member* for `2.abc.def`.\\n\\nNothing admits. But **a plugin now chooses which refusal and which exit status\\nthe host reports**, and nothing measures it.\\n\\nThe reviewer applied and validated the fix: `major = math.MaxInt; continue`\\ninstead of the early return restores the documented classification, keeps F2\\nclosed, and the whole provhost suite still passes.\\n\\nThree things to do:\\n\\n1. validate the whole `X.Y.Z` shape before reporting a recognized major;\\n2. add a named `DecodeResponse` row for `<giant>.abc.def` and `<giant>..0`\\n   asserting `provider_protocol_error` exit 13, alongside the existing exit-6\\n   rows for all-numeric giants, so the two classes are **pinned apart**;\\n3. correct the \\\"no gate was weakened\\\" sentence in the outcome. State the\\n   intended 13→6 arm shift as measured, and stop citing the branch census as\\n   evidence for classification stability.\\n\\n## Why this is marked repeat-of rev1/F3\\n\\nSame class, new site: a shipped claim asserted from a **proxy signal** rather\\nthan measured. Round 1 justified a bound with a fact that turned out false;\\nround 2 justified classification stability with a branch census.\\n===DIRECTIVES===\\nActive Goal: none (run is not goal-bound)\\nNo directives recorded for RUN-260906-a287a1\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3247,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 812,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
