d census\\n27:### 2249 — CI gates leaf round 2: five review findings closed, all claims reproduce\\n58:### 2105 — secconftest round-2 rework: C1–C4 closed, instrument stops reporting untrue things\\n59:- SCOPE: TASK-260830-7a0s2c round-2 (review-verdict-rev1, C1–C4 blocking). Production (test instrument) only in `internal/secconftest`: `crash.go` (finalize gate + `ErrRollbackPastFinalize`, `RemainingArmed`), `skip.go` (`Report()` over live counters, real `mkfifo` fifo probe), `skip_fifo_unix/windows.go` (new, `makeFifo` + fault seam), `hostile.go` untouched, `fuzz_test.go` (no-op poles), `doc.go` (bounds). Leaf-1 `internal/secprim` untouched (`git diff HEAD -- internal/secprim` empty).\\n72:- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest.md` (6/6 AC rows with call sites; digest `5569f34caab734eb` x3). CORRECTION (round-3): the mutant counts and the darwin skip citation first written here (10-row table, 10/10 killed, skipped=0) were disproven in round-1 review and are superseded by the round-2 rework entry above and `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest-round2.md` (29 applied / 2 survivors with bounds; per-test `--- SKIP` lines as the datum).\\n85:### 1553 — Shared-environment boundary round-2 rework: admit hole closed by delegation, shape census, 27-mutant battery\\n86:- SCOPE: TASK-260830-3bkz0c round-2 rework (review-verdict-rev3, B1/B2/F1/F2 blocking + B2b). Freeze on sessadapter/dirnode production lifted for exactly this fix. Production: sessadapter/dirnode decodeStrictObject delegate frame verdicts to environ.DecodeStrictObject (fault translation only); buggy hasLoneSurrogateEscape/readUTF16Escape copies deleted; environ.rawUint53 hardened with trailing-data check; dead environ.validCapability deleted. Tests: frame corpus proves both directions (3 composed rows added, 7 verdicts flipped with absent-phrase pins), shape census (25 rows) + 14 synthetic controls + grammar fresh-name rule + delegation pin, environ unit tests for uint53/sorted-strings-halves/Fault rendering, both leaves' arm censuses derive the bridge from environ source.\\n105:### 1035 — Directory-node leaf round-2 rework: rev1 B1/B2/B3 closed, 185-mutant battery\\n107:- SCOPE: TASK-260830-ljkj8r round-2 rework (review-verdict-rev1, changes requested, B1–B3 blocking). Test-only additions inside `internal/dirnode/` (`bound_census_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `query_operations_test.go`, `arm_identity_test.go`) plus four one-line fixture-surgery fixes (`query_test.go` unknown_field + missing caller, `manifest_test.go` missing member, `probe_test.go` missing member) and three edge extensions (findings 4097, cursor 1/1024 admission, projection bound edges). No production behavior change. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n140:- FIX (B1): `checkValidateResult` no longer calls `checkValidateNullability` — the pinned §7.8 validate success member list names no target members, so the request-body nullability rule cannot apply to successes. Archive-mode validate success now passes through `CheckSuccessBody`; `TestValidateSuccessAdmitsEveryMode` drives staged/live/archive successes. The round-2 anomaly below is resolved, not decided: the document's own success-body list settles it.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 16296,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 4074,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
